{"name":"Mandrake","hex":"#8889a0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mandrake","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant of the genus Mandragora, certain of which are said to have medicinal or aphrodisiac properties; the root of these plants often resembles the shape of a small person, hence occasioning various mythic, magical, or occult uses.","A root of a mandrake plant that resembled human form, especially one kept or used for magic or occult purposes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mandrake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mandrake","blocks":[{"text":"A mandrake is one of several toxic plant species with \"man-shaped\" roots and some uses in folk remedies. The roots by themselves may also be referred to as \"mandrakes\". The term primarily refers to nightshades of the genus Mandragora found in the Mediterranean region."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Mandragoras_454_Dodoens_1583.png/330px-Mandragoras_454_Dodoens_1583.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mandrake","wikidata":"Q2651366"},{"title":"Mandrake (Japanese band)","blocks":[{"text":"Mandrake (マンドレイク) was a Japanese progressive rock band formed in Tokyo in 1973. One of the few Japanese groups active during the genre's heyday, they distinguished themselves by developing a style of their own, harder than the jazz fusion hybrid most other Japanese groups played."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mandrake_(Japanese_band)","wikidata":"Q11341611"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Mandragora_autumnalis1432.JPG/500px-Mandragora_autumnalis1432.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Mandragora_autumnalis1432.JPG/500px-Mandragora_autumnalis1432.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th